description: Write a plan doc before non-trivial multi-step tasks and record divergences after
---

# Plan documentation policy

Before starting any non-trivial task — anything that touches multiple
files, changes project configuration (Dockerfile, devcontainer.json,
next.config.js, CI, auth, build tooling), or involves more than a couple
of steps — create a plan file at:

`.cursor/plans/YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.plan.md`

Use the current date and a short kebab-case description of the task
(e.g. `2026-08-01-playwright-e2e-setup.plan.md`). Skip this for trivial
changes (typo fixes, small copy edits, single-line tweaks).

Cursor’s “Save to workspace” may create a hash-suffixed name like
`name_hash.plan.md`. Rename promptly to the date-prefixed form (same day
as plan creation).

## Plan file structure

```md
---
name: Short title
overview: One–two sentence summary.
todos:
  - id: example
    content: Concrete task
    status: pending   # → completed | cancelled when done
isProject: false
---

# <Task title>

## Goal
What this task is trying to accomplish and why.

## Approach
The proposed approach. Note alternatives considered and why they were
rejected, if relevant. Optional mermaid diagram.

## Implementation
Numbered steps with file paths and concrete changes.

## Out of scope
What this pass explicitly skips.

## Divergences
(Fill during/after execution)
None | or bullets for unplanned decisions, errors, workarounds, or
follow-ups that were not in Approach / Implementation / todos.
```

## Rules

- Write Goal, Approach, Implementation, Out of scope, and todos *before*
  making changes, not retroactively.
- Track completion via frontmatter todo `status` (`completed` /
  `cancelled` / `pending`). No separate Outcome section.
- After the task is done (or abandoned), fill `## Divergences` — use
  `None` if nothing diverged; do not skip the section.
- Never delete or overwrite a previous plan file. Each task gets its own
  file, permanently kept for history.
- After adding a new plan file, add or update a one-line entry in
  `.cursor/plans/README.md` (create it if missing) linking to the file,
  so past plans can be scanned without opening each one individually.
- Plan files are committed to git, not gitignored.
